Today this is mostly inert. The missing laws either cannot fire through their set's input or would duplicate PAR kills. The extra L_rt_go_* can count only through a K2 proof loss attributed at set level, which is not localized to the mutated edge. Derive all eight sets with one rule:
- M0 laws whose statement calls a role in mutant.edges (dec_go implies ok_go);
- M1x laws whose recorded cone names one of the mutant's actions;
- M2 laws whose DERIVATION entry points include one of the mutant's actions.
